  ('durga-devimahatmya-semantic-madhu-kaitabha-episode-en', 'Within this exact provider-revision boundary, Devī Māhātmya chapter 81 presents the narrative of the Goddess acting so that Madhu and Kaiṭabha might be slain.', 'en', 0.9, 'c7fe701aedeedffde57a51b21aa4f8fec697a7922939fb59ffa985e22cc9b7ae', 68, 81, 68, 68, '9674ccdc9085abf16771972b1a0baf50062d4fb67a85864a5a1330d105d9ce3e', 'Tāmasī is translated as dark while retaining the Sanskrit category in Hindi; it should not be reduced to a moral judgment.', 'Devam source-bounded narrative index for one exact Sanskrit Wikisource provider revision at chapter 81, verse 68. It is not a source-original translation, identified print edition, critical recension, complete Devimahatmya or Shakta tradition, festival origin, ritual authority, historical claim, or label for living people or groups.'),
  ('durga-devimahatmya-semantic-madhu-kaitabha-episode-hi', 'इस सटीक प्रदाता-संशोधन सीमा में देवीमाहात्म्य का अध्याय 81 देवी द्वारा मधु और कैटभ के वध की दिशा में किए गए कार्य का आख्यान प्रस्तुत करता है।', 'hi', 0.9, 'c7fe701aedeedffde57a51b21aa4f8fec697a7922939fb59ffa985e22cc9b7ae', 68, 81, 68, 68, '9674ccdc9085abf16771972b1a0baf50062d4fb67a85864a5a1330d105d9ce3e', 'Tāmasī is translated as dark while retaining the Sanskrit category in Hindi; it should not be reduced to a moral judgment.', 'Devam source-bounded narrative index for one exact Sanskrit Wikisource provider revision at chapter 81, verse 68. It is not a source-original translation, identified print edition, critical recension, complete Devimahatmya or Shakta tradition, festival origin, ritual authority, historical claim, or label for living people or groups.'),
  ('durga-devimahatmya-semantic-mahishasura-episode-en', 'Within this exact provider-revision boundary, Devī Māhātmya chapter 83 presents the Goddess''s destruction of Mahiṣa together with his army and allies.', 'en', 0.97, 'c7fe701aedeedffde57a51b21aa4f8fec697a7922939fb59ffa985e22cc9b7ae', 189, 83, 41, 189, '0acdefb9b761bf80c8c2d9a31f26859889e3c67dcf77646e312284e4215acda3', 'The narrative’s trilokya-delusion claim remains explicitly attributed to this source.', 'Devam source-bounded narrative index for one exact Sanskrit Wikisource provider revision at chapter 83, verse 41. It is not a source-original translation, identified print edition, critical recension, complete Devimahatmya or Shakta tradition, festival origin, ritual authority, historical claim, or label for living people or groups.'),
